The [[2015 Copa América]] was an international football tournament held in Chile from 11 June to 4 July 2015. All twelve national teams involved in the tournament were required to register a squad of 22 players, or 23 players if the team chose to have three goalkeepers; only players in these squads were eligible to take part in the tournament. Each nation's squad of players were given shirt numbers 1–23.

== Group A ==

=== Chile ===
The final 23-player squad was announced on 30 May 2015. On 5 June 2015, midfielder [[Edson Puch]] was ruled out of the tournament due to muscle tear, being replaced by [[Francisco Silva (footballer, born 1986)|Francisco Silva]].<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.anfp.cl/noticia/24035/jugador-convocado-a-la-seleccion-chilena|title=JUGADOR CONVOCADO A LA SELECCIÓN CHILENA|date=5 June 2015|access-date=5 June 2015|publisher=ANFP|archive-date=3 March 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303202353/http://www.anfp.cl/noticia/24035/jugador-convocado-a-la-seleccion-chilena|url-status=dead}}</ref> [[José Pedro Fuenzalida]] also replaced the injured [[Carlos Carmona]] on 7 June 2015.<ref>{{cite news|title=Fuenzalida replaces injured Carmona in Chile's Copa América squad |url=http://www.ca2015.com/en/news/fuenzalida-replaces-carmona-in-chiles-copa-america-squad/108k4m6dh5bwc1k9a953dk8ap3 |access-date=17 November 2015 |publisher=ca2015.com |date=7 June 2015 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20151119170852/http://www.ca2015.com/en/news/fuenzalida-replaces-carmona-in-chiles-copa-america-squad/108k4m6dh5bwc1k9a953dk8ap3 |archive-date=19 November 2015 }}</ref>

